[2026-09-06T10:34:29.116Z] [8a2253e7-6195-4067-b209-1a69073a00d4] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=2 | score=68 | rootCause=The render is structurally close to the plan, but the actual execution is weakened by obvious on-screen text timing/placement issues, a long middle that repeats process shots without enough narrative progression, and a CTA that is visually cramped and partially awkwardly wrapped. The reel also appears to underdeliver on the planned audio finish and premium polish, so it reads more like a rough assembly than a finished commercial. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Typography","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The opening text is oversized and visually heavy, competing with the flame action instead of supporting it.","fix":"Reduce text scale, move it lower or center-safe with more breathing room, and limit it to 2-3 words at a time with lighter weight."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Typography","timestamp_seconds":12,"problem":"The CTA text is cramped and awkwardly wrapped across multiple lines, making the ending feel unpremium and harder to read instantly.","fix":"Use a single compact CTA lockup with fewer words, larger margins, and a more elegant line break. Keep the brand name and location distinct from the action line."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Pacing","timestamp_seconds":4.5,"problem":"The middle section overextends the prep/slicing material, creating a repetitive visual rhythm rather than a fast escalation.","fix":"Trim the hand-prep section aggressively and move to the slicing/plating/payoff faster."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Audio","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The render does not convincingly communicate a finished commercial audio experience; the planned SFX/music finish is not evident from the execution audit.","fix":"Treat the audio as non-reliable unless clearly audible in render. Recut so the visuals carry the ad even without SFX dependency; if audio exists, mix it more deliberately with a single strong end hit."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Continuity","timestamp_seconds":1.5,"problem":"Several adjacent frames in the prep section feel nearly identical, reducing perceived progression.","fix":"Use fewer frames from the same source window and cut on more visible action changes."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Brand","timestamp_seconds":12,"problem":"Brand presence is late and functional only; it lacks a truly premium branded hero moment.","fix":"Bring the brand lockup onto a cleaner frame and simplify the final frame so the restaurant name lands with confidence."}]
